<title>ITALY: San Paolo denies interest in Banco Sicilia.</title>
<headline>San Paolo denies interest in Banco Sicilia.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's largest bank San Paolo di Torino denied that it is interested in acquiring a controlling stake in fellow bank Banco di Sicilia.</p>
<p>In a brief statement, the bank's chairman Gianni Zandano denied press reports on Friday that San Paolo was interested in the bank.</p>
<p>&quot;In reference to the press stories today, the Istituto Bancario San Paolo di Torino states that it has not acquired nor is going to acquire the control of Banco di Sicilia,&quot; Zandano said in the statement.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
